Compile/run:
     - Compile using
            make zap
     - run by 
            ./zap [zap | unzap] inputFile outputFile


Program Purpose: To either compress some inputted text into a binary bit string 
*               using the Huffman Coding process or decompress a binary bit
*               string into its original text form. 


Acknowledgements: Nadia helped me with some errors and autograder not working. 

Files: 
main.cpp:
    Main file simple driver function that calls either the encode or decode
    functions depending on the users run command.

HuffmanCoder.cpp:
    Implementation of HuffmanCoder class. Main functionality is to process take
    the inputted text and either build a tree and use it to encode the text, or
    take the inputted string to decode it and turn it into its original text.
HuffmanCoder.h 
    Interfance of the HuffmanCoder.cpp file. Shows the user all the availble 
    functions to call and the public varibales. The code takes in an inputed 
    text and either encodes it into a binary string using the Huffman Coding 
    method or decodes an input binary string using the Huffman Coding method. 
HuffmanTreeNode.h 
BinaryIO.h 
Makefile
    compiles the code.
